published with lightonai/LightOnOCR-3-0.8B and lightonai/LightOnOCR-3-4B.

The image built from Dockerfile.openvino additionally contains, unmodified:
  - the OpenVINO 2026.4.1 runtime library and its Intel GPU plugin (Intel,
    Apache-2.0) and oneTBB (Apache-2.0), copied from Intel's release archive;
    their licence texts and third-party notices are in
    /usr/share/licenses/grpc-lighton-ocr/openvino-licensing;
  - as distribution packages that keep their own licence files under
    /usr/share/doc: the Intel compute runtime for OpenCL, intel-opencl-icd,
    with the Intel Graphics Compiler it depends on (MIT), and the OpenCL ICD
    loader, ocl-icd (BSD-2-Clause).
llama.cpp (MIT) supplies the ggml OpenVINO backend that is compiled into the
server in that image.
